    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling leverage against vulnerable pitching staffs. The cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive attack is **Brice Turang**, who headlines the roster with a 75.06 efficiency score; assuming he anchors the three-hole, he is perfectly positioned to feast on Meibrys Kelly\u2019s 5.47 xERA. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** is a Tier-1 start (73.47) today. His matchup against Brandon Woodruff is aided by a 100% stolen base success rate probability against the starter\u2019s slow delivery, making him the primary engine for our scarcest category. **Josh Naylor** also cracks the 70+ elite threshold (70.49), as his dynamic platoon advantage against Shane Bieber\u2019s high xERA allows him to capitalize on a favorable park factor and strong skill correlation.\n\nWhile the top of the order is solidified, the decision to bench **Cole Young** (48.12) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he benefits from the same favorable matchup against Bieber as **Josh Naylor**, the optimizer prioritized the volume and platoon utility provided by **Alex Freeland** and **Dalton Rushing**. Though **Alex Freeland** faces a lower individual score of 49.35 due to an unfavorable lineup spot, his switch-hitting versatility against Wandy Peralta remains essential for balance. We are also closely monitoring **Brice Turang**\u2019s official lineup status; should his placement shift, we may see volatility in his efficiency. Elsewhere, **James Wood** (51.23) and **Zach McKinstry** (51.76) remain in the lineup despite challenging pitching matchups because their sprint profiles remain essential to our SB-chasing strategy. Proceed with caution on **Dalton Rushing** and **Austin Riley**, as their sub-50 scores suggest limited upside unless the game script forces high-leverage plate appearances.",
